# Settings for us-bins-2026-08-22.csv.
#
# Trusted ABOVE binlist-data.csv, which sits at 0.5. Where the two name a
# different bank for the same BIN, this file is the answer and the archive is
# kept as recorded dissent rather than discarded.
#
# That ranking is evidence-based, not a preference. The archive was published
# in 2020 and has been read-only since; this list is dated 2026-08-22, and the
# disagreements between them are dominated by renames and mergers the archive
# predates — WACHOVIA where this says WELLS FARGO, FAA C.U. where this says
# TRUE SKY C.U., KERN SCHOOLS F.C.U. where this says VALLEY STRONG C.U.
#
# To reverse that, put this below 0.5. Nothing else changes and nothing is
# lost either way: the losing side stays on record and `origin <bin>` shows it.
#
# The `notes` column carries the LEVEL and BANK columns exactly as the source
# printed them, before they were split apart. The reader never ingests it, so
# it costs nothing and every split stays checkable against what was read.
# bintel: confidence = 0.9
